s a series of experiments that eventually shaped how players would move through the world. This stage of development was all about movement, controls, and bringing our main character to life.The First MovementThe first goal was simple: create a player e","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-17T21:27:17Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706685665","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:36:03Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4654750-1846651706682948","game_id":"steam-4654750","kind":"announcement","title":"Devlog #1 — The First Spark: Building the Foundation","summary":"Every game begins with an idea. For Quiet Time, that idea came from wanting to rethink some of the familiar conventions of survival games.I had always been interested in survival games, but I wanted to explore something different from the traditional formula of gathering wood, keeping a fire alive, and fighting enemies with conventional weapons. What if survival depended on something entirely different? What if sound, rather than fire or weapons, became the player's greatest tool for staying ali","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-16T19:55:27Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706682948","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:36:03Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-4654750":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T13:16:54Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:16:53Z","error_codes":[]}},"news_last_attempt_at":{"steam-4654750":"2026-10-26T13:16:54Z"},"notices":[],"news_sources":{"4654750":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T13:16:53Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-26T13:16:53Z","status":"ok","error_codes":[],"last_fulltext_checked_at":"2026-10-26T13:16:53Z"},"5417690":{"last_attempt_